  "goodToKnow": "Die Laterne is a lantern or street lamp: die Straßenlaterne. Around St Martin's Day (11 November), German children make paper lanterns and walk in a Laternenumzug, singing songs like Laterne, Laterne, Sonne, Mond und Sterne. In sport, die rote Laterne means last place in the table. Lili Marleen, the famous WWII song, begins by a lantern at the barracks gate. Plural: die Laternen."
